      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redfern%2C_New_South_Wales"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1945 Bill Onus founded the Redfern All‑Blacks Rugby League team, a community and political force through the 1950s and 1960s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.niaa.gov.au/sites/default/files/publications/indigenous/empowered-communities/alt/description-redfern.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1970s saw Aboriginal‑founded services—Medical, Legal, and Housing Companies—established in Redfern, sparking nationwide self‑determination.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.niaa.gov.au/sites/default/files/publications/indigenous/empowered-communities/alt/description-redfern.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Redfern became the birthplace of Australia’s urban Aboriginal civil rights movement from the 1960s through the 1990s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.niaa.gov.au/sites/default/files/publications/indigenous/empowered-communities/alt/description-redfern.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Redfern railway station, the first stop south of Central, sits on the western edge of the suburb.",
